<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51420" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰύζω</span></b> , aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴυξα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.237
				</span></i>
			:—<i>shout, yell</i>, in order to scare beasts, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ μάλ᾽ ἰύζουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.66
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ ἰύζοντες ἕποντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.162
				</span></i>
			; later, <i>yell</i> from grief or pain, <i>cry out</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴυξεν ἀφωνήτῳ ἄχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
				</span></i>
			 l.c.; used by <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i> in lyr., only in imper., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴυζ᾽ ἄποτμον βοάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Pers.</u>
					281
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				1042
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				808
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				872
			</span></i>; part., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰύζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					787
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰύζων ἀν᾽ ὄρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					512
				</span></i>
			 (perh. here =
			<i>piping</i>, cf. sq.); of bees, <i>buzz</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				1.440
			</span></i>. (From the Interjection <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰΰ</span>, q.v. (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰού</span>
			acc. to <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				480.6
			</span></i>): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝι-</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀβίυκτος, ἐκβιούζει.ʼ [ῑ</span>
			
				Ep.
			 and <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				787
			</span></i>, and prob. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>]</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
